      "content": "There is no rule requiring a dramatic arc or redemption for Elias; in fact, stories hissed with despair and psychological depth do very well without a happy ending if the goal is to explore genuine human frailty. It is perfectly realistic and powerful for Elias to reach that point where holding himself up feels impossible, turning the \"arc\" into a raw depiction of struggle rather than a triumph. Ultimately, these stories resonate precisely because they honor the darkness of existence rather than forcing a forced narrative resolution.",
